The review has been written to `docs/reviews/cross-cutting/xcut-01-equipment-zone-id-propagation.md`.

**Summary**: 8 findings across the zone_id propagation chain:

| Severity | Count | Key issue |
|----------|-------|-----------|
| **Critical** | 1 | Non-baseboard HVAC zone_id _never_ propagated from HPXML — always falls back to `ZoneId(1)` |
| **High** | 2 | Water heater zone_id same gap; the `unwrap_or(ZoneId(1))` fallback silently masks both issues |
| **Medium** | 1 | Battery zone_id optional but HPXML parser never populates it |
| **Low** | 2 | No zone_id=0 leakage confirmed; PV zone=None correct |
| **Info** | 2 | Duct multi-zone routing works; zone topology is immutable |

The core bug is in `resolve_hvac.rs:1693` — `conditioned_zone_id(building)` is only called for Electric Baseboard but not for any other HVAC type. The main recommendation is a one-line change to inject zone_id for all HVAC equipment, plus a water heater analog in `resolve_water_heater.rs`.
